Following up on our architecture discussions for the upcoming Agentic BI & Headless Semantic Layer Proof of Concept (PoC), I have drafted the complete Technical Requirements Document (TRD) for your review.

This PoC focuses on demonstrating an end-to-end, 100% open-source pipeline that enables natural language dashboard generation over a local Lakehouse Gold layer while maintaining single-source metric governance.

Executive Summary & Architectural Stack
The architecture decouples metric governance, reasoning, and visual rendering across six lightweight components:

Storage & Engine: DuckDB reading local Gold Parquet/Delta files.
Headless Semantic Layer: Cube Core defining metrics as code (OSI-aligned) and serving them via REST, Postgres SQL, and MCP endpoints.
Agent Orchestration: LangGraph (Python) driving the catalog search, query execution, and chart spec generation control loop.
LLM Brain: Local Ollama (qwen2.5-coder:7b) with fallback support for OpenAI (gpt-4o-mini).
Dashboard Canvas: Next.js + react-vega dynamically compiling declarative Vega-Lite JSON specs into interactive SVG/Canvas charts.
Traditional BI Comparison: Metabase (Community Edition) connected directly to Cube via its Postgres SQL API to prove metric consistency across both traditional and AI interfaces.
Core Objectives Covered in the TRD
Zero Custom Rendering Code: The frontend canvas renders charts purely from declarative Vega-Lite JSON specs generated by the agent.
Dual-Consumer Validation: Demonstrates that both an AI chat agent and traditional BI dashboards (Metabase) yield identical numeric results from the shared Cube semantic layer.
Turnkey Local Deployment: The entire stack is containerized to run locally via a single docker-compose.yml file with zero cloud dependencies.